---
import ServiceComparison from './ServiceComparison.astro';
import { projects, path } from '../data/profile';
const project = projects.find(project => project.slug === 'stateful-evaluation')!;
const methods = [
  { name: 'Review the playbook', helps: 'Check its structure and intended logic.', gap: 'The service calls and their effects still need to be tested.' },
  { name: 'Supply fixed responses', helps: 'Exercise branches and result handling.', gap: 'Prewritten replies alone do not reproduce changes caused by earlier actions.' },
  { name: 'Run against real services', helps: 'Observe actual integration and service behavior.', gap: 'Prepare service access, test data, and cleanup; VM-based deployments add infrastructure to maintain.' },
];
---
<div class="environment-study" data-study-export>
  <header class="study-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow">ONGOING RESEARCH / SECURITY AUTOMATION</span>
    <h1>AI-built test environments<br /> <em>for security playbooks.</em></h1>
    <p class="study-lead">I build agents that generate disposable service environments for testing AI-created security workflows. The goal is lower-cost, repeatable testing without connecting to live systems.</p>
    <p class="study-context">A playbook is an automated sequence of security actions, such as investigating an alert or disabling an account. Generating the workflow is only part of the job: testing it needs services to interact with.</p>
    <a class="text-link study-jump" href="#concept-demo">See the approach <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
  </header>

  <section class="approach-section" id="concept-demo" aria-label="How the generated environment fits">
    <ServiceComparison />
    <div class="design-goals" aria-label="What the approach is designed to enable">
      <div><span>01 / BUILD</span><h2>Less setup work</h2><p>Agents generate service behavior from connector code and documentation.</p></div>
      <div><span>02 / TEST</span><h2>Observable effects</h2><p>Actions change stored data, so later calls can observe what happened.</p></div>
      <div><span>03 / REPEAT</span><h2>Reset or discard</h2><p>Choose the starting data, reset between tests, or rebuild the environment.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="problem-section" aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
    <div class="section-intro"><span class="eyebrow">THE TESTING GAP</span><h2 id="problem-heading">A workflow needs more<br /> than a test button.</h2><p>Existing methods each cover part of the job. Running a playbook also requires an environment that responds to its actions, with data you can control and restore.</p></div>
    <div class="method-table-wrap">
      <table class="method-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">What existing playbook testing methods cover and what they still require</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Testing method</th><th scope="col">What it helps check</th><th scope="col">What remains</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{methods.map(method => <tr><th scope="row">{method.name}</th><td data-label="What it helps check">{method.helps}</td><td data-label="What remains">{method.gap}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="research-focus"><span class="focus-mark" aria-hidden="true">↳</span><p><strong>My research automates building that environment.</strong> The aim is to reduce the cost of maintaining full service deployments or writing substitutes by hand, while keeping the existing playbook and connector in the test path.</p></div>
    <p class="scope-note">Existing end-to-end tests can verify behavior when supplied with suitable environments and checks. This work targets environment generation; test requirements still determine whether a playbook did the right thing.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="contribution-section" aria-labelledby="contribution-heading">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">MY CONTRIBUTION</span><h2 id="contribution-heading">From service interfaces<br /> to runnable environments.</h2></div>
    <div class="contribution-copy"><p>I develop the agent workflow that analyzes connector actions and their state relationships, generates the service implementation and initial data, and reviews behavior through the real SOAR platform and connector.</p><p class="research-status"><span class="status-label">CURRENT STATUS</span>Ongoing research. Lower setup cost and faster rebuilding are design goals; comparative cost and provisioning-time results are not yet reported.</p></div>
  </section>

  <details class="technical-details">
    <summary>Technical details & research scope</summary>
    <div class="technical-content">
      <p>Pipeline1 is the internal name of this environment-generation workflow. The execution path retains Splunk SOAR, the security automation platform, and its unmodified service connector.</p>
      <ul>{project.approach.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>
      <p>The generated implementation supplies the modeled external-service behavior. Editable seed data initializes a separate runtime state that can be reset between tests. Builder and reviewer agents use behavioral acceptance conditions to guide implementation and repair.</p>
      <p>The environment records action effects; separate task requirements and assertions judge playbook correctness. It does not establish complete equivalence with every behavior of the real service.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <p class="study-download"><a class="text-link" href={path('/pipeline1-concept.svg')} download>Download the overview diagram <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
</div>
<!-- End of portable research story -->

<style>
  .environment-study{max-width:1100px;margin-inline:auto}
  .sr-only{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0}
  .study-heading{padding:22px 0 40px;max-width:1010px}
  .eyebrow{display:block;color:var(--accent);font-size:10px;margin-bottom:20px;letter-spacing:.12em}
  .study-heading h1{font-size:clamp(37px,4.4vw,62px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.055em;font-weight:600}
  .study-heading h1 em{font-style:normal;font-weight:inherit;color:var(--accent)}
  .study-lead{font-size:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-top:24px;max-width:850px;color:var(--text)}
  .study-context{font-size:14px;line-height:1.85;margin-top:16px;max-width:830px;color:var(--muted)}
  .study-jump{font-size:12px;margin-top:22px}
  .approach-section{scroll-margin-top:110px}
  h2{font-size:32px;font-weight:550;letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.2}
  .design-goals{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:32px;padding:28px 0 40px}
  .design-goals>div{border-left:1px solid var(--line);padding-left:18px}.design-goals span{display:block;font-size:9px;color:var(--accent);letter-spacing:.08em;margin-bottom:12px}.design-goals h2{font-size:19px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.design-goals p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted);margin-top:9px;max-width:290px}
  .problem-section{padding:42px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .section-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.1fr;column-gap:65px;align-items:start}.section-intro>.eyebrow{grid-column:1/-1}.section-intro>p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted)}
  .method-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:28px;text-align:left}.method-table th,.method-table td{padding:17px 18px 17px 0;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);line-height:1.8}.method-table thead th{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:500;color:var(--muted);padding-top:0;padding-bottom:13px}.method-table tbody th{font-size:13px;font-weight:550;width:24%;padding-right:25px}.method-table td{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);width:38%}.method-table td:last-child,.method-table thead th:last-child{padding-right:0}
  .research-focus{display:flex;gap:17px;align-items:flex-start;padding:22px 24px;margin-top:24px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 4%,var(--bg));border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 25%,var(--line));border-radius:10px}.focus-mark{font-size:24px;color:var(--accent);line-height:1.4}.research-focus p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted)}.research-focus strong{font-weight:550;color:var(--text);display:block;margin-bottom:4px}.scope-note{font-size:11px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin-top:15px;max-width:950px}
  .contribution-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.1fr;gap:65px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:42px 0}.contribution-copy>p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--muted)}.research-status{margin-top:22px;border-left:2px solid var(--line);padding-left:15px;font-size:12px!important}.status-label{display:block;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:8px}
  .technical-details{border-block:1px solid var(--line)}summary{cursor:pointer;padding:20px 0;font-size:13px;font-weight:500}summary::marker{color:var(--accent)}.technical-content{max-width:850px;padding:0 0 23px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.9}.technical-content ul{padding-left:22px;margin-block:15px}.technical-content li{padding:3px 0}.technical-content p+p{margin-top:14px}.study-download{margin-top:22px}.study-download a{font-size:11px}
  @media(max-width:800px){.section-intro,.contribution-section{column-gap:32px}.study-heading h1{font-size:47px}.study-lead{font-size:18px}.design-goals{gap:20px}h2{font-size:28px}}
  @media(max-width:540px){.study-heading{padding:10px 0 28px}.study-heading h1{font-size:36px}.study-heading h1 br{display:none}.eyebrow{font-size:9px;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px}.study-lead{font-size:16px;margin-top:20px;line-height:1.8}.study-context{font-size:12px}.study-jump{margin-top:17px}.design-goals{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:24px 0 32px;gap:22px}.design-goals span{margin-bottom:7px}.design-goals p{max-width:none;margin-top:6px}.section-intro,.contribution-section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}.section-intro>.eyebrow{margin-bottom:0}.section-intro>p,.contribution-copy>p{font-size:13px}h2{font-size:27px}.problem-section,.contribution-section{padding:32px 0}.method-table th,.method-table td{padding:13px 9px 13px 0}.method-table thead th{font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.025em}.method-table tbody th{font-size:11px;padding-right:10px;width:26%}.method-table td{font-size:10px;line-height:1.8;width:37%}.research-focus{padding:16px 14px;gap:10px}.research-focus p{font-size:12px}.scope-note{font-size:10px}.contribution-section .eyebrow{margin-bottom:14px}.technical-content{font-size:12px}.study-download{margin-top:18px}}
  @media print{.study-heading h1{font-size:30px}.study-lead{font-size:12px}.study-context{font-size:10px}.study-jump,.study-download{display:none}.design-goals{padding-bottom:20px}.problem-section,.contribution-section{padding-block:20px}h2{font-size:22px}.method-table th,.method-table td{font-size:10px;padding-block:10px}}
  @media screen and (max-width:540px){.method-table thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0)}.method-table tbody,.method-table tr{display:block}.method-table tr{padding:16px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.method-table tbody th{display:block;width:auto;padding:0;border:0;font-size:14px}.method-table td{display:block;width:auto;border:0;padding:10px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.8}.method-table td::before{content:attr(data-label);display:block;font-size:8px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:3px}}
</style>
